{"id": "EUVD-2026-82300", "enisaUuid": "46626726-42c6-3f3b-9fef-f41dee85c4f1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/v3d: Clear queue->active_job when v3d_fence_create() fails\n\nThe run_job() callbacks for BIN, RENDER, TFU and CSD assign the incoming\njob to queue->active_job before calling v3d_fence_create(). If\nv3d_fence_create() fails, the callback returns NULL without clearing\nactive_job, leaving a dangling pointer.\n\nCreate a failure path in all run_job() callbacks that clears the active\njob before returning NULL. The BIN path takes queue->queue_lock around the\nclear as it races against v3d_overflow_mem_work(); RENDER, TFU and CSD\npaths have no concurrent reader, so the clear is lock-free.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:12:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:15", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f661f42beb558b2d21882f0cd527ed6c8e7e749", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bdeb73d7312100e00c3e643ff233f09b6ec114aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a8aa74859dd73eaa76c55eb74da708e56ef51c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b9878aba5cf93bc2b55ba9eb807757ce3239bec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/25a1669907512e927fab9ad4d4fb74ff57f63cd9"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93192", "GHSA-58h7-x7wh-hg7q"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "33b2c2fa-bd1e-38f6-b8ad-ccf523d714e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a783a09ee76d6259296dc6aeea2b6884fa526980 <3a8aa74859dd73eaa76c55eb74da708e56ef51c5"}, {"id": "3c6865a2-3cd4-36e5-92a6-c287d4c1d3ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a783a09ee76d6259296dc6aeea2b6884fa526980 <bdeb73d7312100e00c3e643ff233f09b6ec114aa"}, {"id": "3e9357e3-bd92-3ffc-85e0-92b305e7eb19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "661e7b3e-7489-3ff5-a572-8e600a0ee66e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a783a09ee76d6259296dc6aeea2b6884fa526980 <1f661f42beb558b2d21882f0cd527ed6c8e7e749"}, {"id": "6b72ec85-e4c1-3b96-90fa-a9c472ba5b45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "7fca12bd-4aca-386d-8e88-047aaa12e7e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "82d568f1-9b9f-3fbc-9c97-c38da2984e35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "94631eb0-64b1-3232-980f-ab25ee1a1666", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a783a09ee76d6259296dc6aeea2b6884fa526980 <0b9878aba5cf93bc2b55ba9eb807757ce3239bec"}, {"id": "d42f8b73-67e3-3421-92aa-750c3b92d861", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.3"}, {"id": "e715b7a7-8a23-3958-b7d7-ae61b75aaef7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a783a09ee76d6259296dc6aeea2b6884fa526980 <25a1669907512e927fab9ad4d4fb74ff57f63cd9"}, {"id": "f284af16-11a8-318a-8472-43d8a0af3535", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "f7012e0a-e49c-386a-8246-4e7ad7a1e47b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6b6aed74-45a1-3a89-95ac-a9ae535ff59c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}